  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The statement of moseley&#39;s law is: &ldquo;The square root of the frequency of the x-ray emitted by an atom is proportional to its atomic number&rdquo;.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8733;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math>&nbsp;So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Moseley is the scientist most directly responsible for realizing that the structure of the atom is key to understanding the elements themselves.</p>"
  }
